{"page_content": "ACME/Flame Design Final Report (2023) \n \n6 April 2023 \n57 \n \n \nAppendix E. Astronauts who Conducted ISS Operations for Flame \nDesign \nThis list was prepared by Dennis Stocker from his log of ACME operations. \n \nThe Flame Design experiment was supported by ten ISS crew members on 24 separate days, with 13 \noccurring during the first round of operations and 11 in the second round.  The 8 men and 2 women are \nlisted by the number of days in which they conducted supporting on-orbit activities and alphabetically. \n \nCrew member \nYear \nDay(s) of year \n# days \nKoch, Christina (NASA) \n2019 \n095, 099-100, 165, 179, 192, 203 (with Ovchinin) \n7 \nVande Hei, Mark (NASA) \n2021 \n299, 307, 337 (with Dubrov), 344 \n5 \n \n2022 \n005 \nDubrov, Petr (RSA) \n2021 \n337 \n4 \n \n2022 \n024, 026, 031 \nHague, T. Nick (NASA) \n2019 \n140, 151, 164, 198  \n4 \nChari, Raja (NASA) \n2021 \n355 \n2 \n \n2022 \n017 \nSaint-Jacques, David (CSA) \n2019 \n130, 165 \n2 \nKimbrough, Shane (NASA) \n2021 \n306  \n1 \nKononenko, Oleg (RSA) \n2019 \n101 \n1 \nMcArthur, K. Megan (NASA) 2021 \n307 \n1 \nOvchinin, Alexey (RSA) \n2019 \n203 \n1 \n \nTogether, the astronauts and cosmonauts represent three space agencies and three nations, namely \nCanada (CSA), Russia (RSA), and the United States (NASA). \n \n \nAgency \n# crew \nCrew members \n# days for agency \n \nNASA \n6 \nKoch, Vande Hei, Hague, Chari, Kimbrough, McArthur \n19 \n \nRSA \n3 \nDubrov, Kononenko, Ovchinin \n6 \n \nCSA \n1 \nSaint-Jacques \n2 \n \nIn the first round of testing, which featured normal flames, most of the crew tasks were carried out by \nChristina Koch (NASA), Nick Hague (NASA), and David Saint-Jacques (CSA).  In the second round, which \nfeatured inverse flames (except on the first test day), most crew tasks were conducted by Mark Vande \nHei (NASA), Petr Dubrov (RSA), and Raja Chari (NASA).", "metadata": {"source": "PSI-10_Reports_FinalRpt_ACMEFlameDesign.pdf", "page": 57}}